# Walk sweep -- how fast, and which way, does the AC move for a given stick?
#
# mission-1.pad's prefix into the first mission (gameplay from ~poll 2050),
# then thirty-poll holds of the left stick with twenty polls of centre between
# them, kept short and ordered so the AC stays inside the ground the classic
# run proved clear: forward at 127; straight right; forward-left at 30 degrees;
# straight back; forward at 96, 64 and 45. With PSPRECOMP_INPUT_LOG the push
# primitive (host/replacements.c) writes the direction, the cap it asked for
# and the speed reached, every frame:
#
#   scripts/09-replay.sh --decode --env PSPRECOMP_INPUT=dual \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_INPUT_LOG=reports/walk-sweep.log scenarios/walk-sweep.pad
#   scripts/walk-analyze.py reports/walk-sweep.log
#
# The same file under `modern` walks by Y alone and turns by X; under classic
# (PSPRECOMP_INPUT unset) the game thresholds each axis at 100, so 96 and
# below do nothing, the 30-degree push walks straight ahead, and straight
# right is a turn. The position in the log tells a wall from the law: a speed
# that falls back under its cap while the stick holds still is terrain.

drain 500

@76     state circle 128 128   # t=3.080s
@78     state none 128 128   # t=3.160s
@176    state circle 128 128   # t=7.458s
@178    state none 128 128   # t=7.553s
